    {'padas': ['meghāvṛtaṃ niśi na bhāti nabho vitāraṃ', 'nidrābhyupaiti ca hariṃ sukhasevitāram |', 'sendrāyudhaśca jalado dharasannibhānāṃ', 'saṃrambhamāvahati bhūdharasannibhānām'], 'num': '|| 3 ||', 'gloss': 'By night the cloud-covered sky does not shine, starless; sleep comes to Hari, who takes his ease; and the cloud with Indra’s bow, roaring, rouses the fury of elephants that are like mountains. (The third quarter is translated from the usual text, jalado’dya rasann ibhānām; the print’s reading gives no sense.)'},
    {'padas': ['sataḍijjaladārpitaṃ nageṣu svanadambhodharabhītapannageṣu |', 'paridhīraravaṃ jalaṃ darīṣu prapatatyadbhutarūpasundarīṣu'], 'num': '|| 4 ||', 'gloss': 'Water, brought by the lightning-bearing clouds, falls on the mountains where serpents cower from the thundering clouds, with a deep, circling roar, into the caves that are beautiful with their strange forms.'},
    {'padas': ["kṣipraṃ prasādayati samprati ko'pi tāni", 'kāntāmukhāni rativigrahakopitāni |', 'utkaṇṭhayanti pathikān jaladāḥ svanantaḥ', 'śokaḥ samudbhavati tadvanitāsvanantaḥ'], 'num': '|| 5 ||', 'gloss': 'Now some man quickly softens the faces of his beloveds, angered by love’s quarrel; the thundering clouds make the travellers long for home, and endless grief rises in their wives.'},
    {'padas': ['chādite dinakarasya bhāvane', 'khājjale patati śokabhāvane |', 'manmathe ca hṛdi hantumudyate', 'proṣitapramadayedamudyate'], 'num': '|| 6 ||', 'gloss': 'When the sun’s radiance is hidden, when water falls from the sky and breeds grief, when Love rises to strike at the heart, a woman whose husband is away speaks thus:'},
    {'padas': ['sarvakālamavalaṅghya toyadā', 'āgatāḥ stha dayito gato yadā |', 'niṣṭhureṇa paradeśasevinā', 'mārayiṣyatha hatena māṃ vinā'], 'num': '|| 7 ||', 'gloss': 'O clouds, passing over every other season you have come just when my beloved is gone; you will be the death of me, left without that cruel wretch who keeps to foreign lands.'},
    {'padas': ['brūta taṃ pathikapāṃśulaṃ ghanāḥ', 'yūyameva pathi śīghralaṅghanāḥ |', 'anyadeśaratiradya mucyatāṃ', 'sāthavā tava vadhūḥ kimucyatām'], 'num': '|| 8 ||', 'gloss': 'Tell that rake of a traveller, O clouds — you are the ones who cross the road swiftly: “Give up today your love of another land; or else, what is to be said to that wife of yours?”'},
